    "title": "Shortest Subarray Reaching a Target",
    "description": "Given values, return the smallest length of a nonempty contiguous subarray whose sum is at least target. Return -1 when no such subarray exists. Only the length is returned, so equally short subarrays need no tie rule. values contains 0 to 2000 integers, each between -1000000 and 1000000; target is an integer between 1 and 2000000000. Negative values are allowed. An empty input always returns -1, and the empty subarray is never eligible. Aim for O(n) time with prefix sums and a monotonic deque; a window that assumes all values are positive is insufficient.",
