  "referenceSolutions": {
    "javascript": "export function shortestSubarrayAtLeastTarget(values          , target        )         {\n  const prefix           = [0];\n  for (const value of values) prefix.push(prefix[prefix.length - 1] + value);\n  const deque           = [];\n  let head = 0, best = values.length + 1;\n  for (let i = 0; i < prefix.length; i++) {\n    while (head < deque.length && prefix[i] - prefix[deque[head]] >= target) {\n      best = Math.min(best, i - deque[head]);\n      head++;\n    }\n    while (head < deque.length && prefix[deque[deque.length - 1]] >= prefix[i]) deque.pop();\n    deque.push(i);\n  }\n  return best <= values.length ? best : -1;\n}\n",
    "typescript": "export function shortestSubarrayAtLeastTarget(values: number[], target: number): number {\n  const prefix: number[] = [0];\n  for (const value of values) prefix.push(prefix[prefix.length - 1] + value);\n  const deque: number[] = [];\n  let head = 0, best = values.length + 1;\n  for (let i = 0; i < prefix.length; i++) {\n    while (head < deque.length && prefix[i] - prefix[deque[head]] >= target) {\n      best = Math.min(best, i - deque[head]);\n      head++;\n    }\n    while (head < deque.length && prefix[deque[deque.length - 1]] >= prefix[i]) deque.pop();\n    deque.push(i);\n  }\n  return best <= values.length ? best : -1;\n}\n"
  },
  "explanation": "Construct prefix sums and keep candidate prefix indices in increasing order of both index and prefix value. For each new prefix, remove eligible candidates from the front while recording their subarray lengths: a future endpoint cannot improve a length already found for that candidate. Remove candidates from the back whose prefix value is at least the new prefix, because the newer index yields at least as large a sum with a shorter length for every future endpoint. Then append the new index. Each index is appended and removed at most once, giving O(n) time and O(n) auxiliary space. Prefix sums have magnitude at most 2000000000 under these bounds and remain exact safe integers."
